# Security Rules

## Input Validation
- Validate all user inputs on both client and server
- Sanitize data before database operations
- Use proper type checking and validation libraries
- Implement CSRF protection

## Authentication & Authorization
- Always verify user authentication before protected operations
- Use proper session management
- Implement proper logout functionality
- Check user permissions for all operations

```typescript
// ✅ Good authentication check
export async function createPost(data: PostData) {
  const { data: { user }, error } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
  
  if (error || !user) {
    throw new Error('Authentication required')
  }
  
  // Proceed with authenticated operation
}
```

## Environment Variables
- Never commit secrets to version control
- Use proper environment variable validation
- Use different configurations for different environments
- Rotate secrets regularly

## Data Protection
- Use HTTPS in production
- Implement proper CORS policies
- Sanitize user-generated content
- Use proper database permissions (RLS)

## Error Handling
- Don't expose sensitive information in error messages
- Log errors securely
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use generic error messages for users